// =============================================================================
// leasing-tenants-course — "Leasing and Tenant Selection"
// =============================================================================
// Course four of the Real Estate department. DR-0500 established whose the
// ground is, DR-0501 what faithful management is measured by, DR-0504 how the
// transaction is done honestly. This one covers the part with a PERSON on the
// other side of it -- who you let in, how you decide, what the paper says, and
// what happens when it goes wrong.
//
// THE ARC, one argument in eight moves:
//   1. Ye know the heart of a stranger (Exodus 23:9; Deuteronomy 10:18-19)
//   2. The gold ring and the vile raiment (James 2:1-4, 9)
//   3. He that answereth a matter before he heareth it (Proverbs 18:13, 17)
//   4. Read the covenant in their hearing (Exodus 24:3, 7)
//   5. Wherein shall he sleep? (Exodus 22:26-27)
//   6. Every man under his own vine (Micah 4:4)
//   7. Go and tell him between thee and him alone (Matthew 18:15-16)
//   8. As much as lieth in you, live peaceably (Romans 12:18; Galatians 6:9-10)
//
// Remember the position -> refuse the seating chart -> hear the matter before
// answering it -> put the terms in their hearing -> know what the pledge costs
// them at night -> aim at the state the Word aims at -> escalate privately and
// in steps -> and accept the limit: as much as lieth in YOU, which is not all
// of it. Lesson 8 is last because every course in this department has ended by
// naming what the steward controls and what he does not.
//
// WHY THIS COURSE EXISTS IN THIS FORM. A tenant is a stranger in the precise
// sense Scripture uses: new to the street, without standing there, dependent on
// someone who has both. That is the one class of person Yahweh commands with a
// reason attached to MEMORY -- you were that, so you know how it feels. The
// department has named a recurring defect three times now (the false weight,
// the lawful process that took Naboth's vineyard, attrition on a promise): a
// wrong that is invisible from inside any single instance. James 2 is the same
// defect wearing clothes. Seat the well-dressed man well and the poor man
// badly, and no single seating is a crime; the pattern is the sin, and the Word
// names it as one: "ye commit sin, and are convinced of the law as
// transgressors" (James 2:9).
//
// THE LINE THIS COURSE HOLDS (DR-0098, DR-0100). Screening a tenant on the
// facts -- what they earn, whether they paid before, what a prior landlord
// says -- is not respect of persons; it is the diligence lesson 3 commands.
// Deciding by appearance is. Both edges are taught, neither is softened, and
// the course does not stage the two as a debate for the reader to settle.
//
// NO PASSAGE IS SHARED with the department's other three courses, and the
// course test CHECKS that against their own reference lists rather than
// trusting it.
//
// AGE BANDS FROM THE FIRST COMMIT (DR-0497 / DR-0498): every lesson carries
// levels.teen and levels.senior, authored rather than re-registered.
//
// VERIFICATION (DR-0076 / SCRIPTURE-REFERENCE-STANDARD). All 60 quoted spans
// were fetched VERBATIM from the repository's own KJV and the generator refused
// to emit until every one matched. Our prose says Yahweh; quotations keep
// "the LORD" and "God" exactly as the KJV has them (DR-0210's bright line).
// The generator's own elision check was WRONG when this course was built -- it
// ran from one closing quote to the next opening one and so flagged an ellipsis
// in our own prose between two quotations, which DR-0459 permits. Fixed to test
// each quoted span on its own, and proven to still catch a real elision in both
// the ASCII and the Unicode form before it was trusted.
//
// AND THE HEADER'S OWN CLAIMS WERE AUDITED. This comment block named James
// 2:9, Exodus 24:3 and Galatians 6:9 in the arc while the lesson bodies never
// quoted any of the three -- a claim without evidence (DR-0076 section 1) in
// our own file header, caught by the course test rather than by reading. Each
// was added to the lesson it belonged to, through the same verbatim gate:
// James names partiality as SIN, the covenant assent was taken TWICE (and the
// second time after a reading), and weariness rather than corruption is how a
// steward stops doing his half.
//
// TEACHING, NOT LEGAL ADVICE -- carried on the meta, and it matters more here
// than anywhere else in the department: fair-housing law, screening rules,
// security-deposit limits, notice periods and eviction procedure are state
// specific, they change, and getting them wrong is actionable.
// =============================================================================

