    bigIdea: 'Paul closes the matter with a sentence built out of two limits and one absolute: "If it be possible, as much as lieth in you, live peaceably with all men" (Romans 12:18). IF IT BE POSSIBLE — sometimes it is not, and Scripture says so rather than pretending. AS MUCH AS LIETH IN YOU — your portion, not the other party’s. And then WITH ALL MEN — no category excluded, including the tenant who lied, the one who left the unit wrecked, and the one taking you to court. The limits are on the outcome; there is no limit on who it applies to.',
    inApp: 'Name the hardest tenancy you are in right now — the person you least want to deal with. Write two columns: what lies in YOU (a call returned, a number stated honestly, a deduction evidenced, a promise kept) and what does not (their choices, their story to others, the outcome). Do everything in the first column this week and stop measuring yourself by the second.',
    anchor: { ref: 'Romans 12:18', theme: '"If it be possible, as much as lieth in you, live peaceably with all men." Two honest limits and one unlimited demand: peace may not be possible, it may not be within your power — and what IS in your power is required, with ALL men.' },
